<!-- Bottom-nav "Settings" glyph, active/filled state.

     Geometry is character-for-character ic_nav_settings_outline.xml - same
     gear path, same 1.8 stroke. The stroke moves from fm_ink_dim to
     fm_primary and the transparent fill becomes fm_primary, so the outer
     silhouette does not move between states (it previously shrank 0.6dp on
     selection). See the Design Decisions Log in Confluence, "Selected nav
     glyphs keep their stroke" (2026-09-22), and DESIGN-SYSTEM-PHASE3.md
     6.9/6.9a.

     FRM-125 / GH #160 (this migration): moved from a 24x24 viewport /
     strokeWidth 1.0 to 28x28 / strokeWidth 1.8, matching ic_nav_groups_*
     (1.9) and ic_nav_history_* (1.8) so all three bottom-nav marks render
     at the same visual weight under the shared 28dp itemIconSize - the
     gear previously rendered at ~1.17dp effective stroke, about a third
     lighter than its neighbours. Path coordinates were scaled by 7/6 with
     a script (not retyped by hand); strokeWidth was set explicitly to
     match History rather than scaled, per §6.9. The inner circle's
     centring on the cog body - a defect once already - was re-verified
     after the rescale.

     INVARIANT (§6.9a): the selected silhouette must be a strict superset
     of the unselected one - zero pixels lost at any edge. -->
